# Binaries git must not touch.
#
# Without this, `git add document/*.pdf` warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF
# the next time Git touches it" — and it means it. Every 0x0A byte inside the
# PDF becomes 0x0D 0x0A on checkout, the xref offsets in the trailer stop
# pointing at the objects they name, and the file that opens fine here fails
# to open on a fresh clone. The same holds for every other format below.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
*.m4a   binary
*.webm  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.node  binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.dmg   binary
